<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Contractor agreement' }) %>
<div class="card" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto">
  <h1>Contractor agreement</h1>
  <p class="muted">Version <%= version %>. DRAFT for legal review before use.</p>
  <h3>1. The parties</h3>
  <p>This agreement is between <strong><%= company.legal_name %></strong> (NZBN <%= company.nzbn %>), trading as <strong><%= company.trading_name %></strong> ("Ridgeline"), and the contractor business applying ("you").</p>
  <h3>2. Independent contractor</h3>
  <p>You provide services as an independent business, not as an employee. You decide whether to accept each job offer, supply your own tools, vehicle and staff, and are responsible for your own tax, ACC levies, insurance and health and safety obligations. Nothing in this agreement guarantees you any volume of work.</p>
  <h3>3. Compliance</h3>
  <p>You must hold and keep current public liability insurance and any licence your trade requires (for example EWRB or PGDB registration), and upload evidence before receiving offers. Offers stop automatically if a document expires.</p>
  <h3>4. Accepting and doing jobs</h3>
  <p>Accepted jobs must be attended within the job's service-level target shown on the offer. You record arrival, work start and completion in the app, upload before and after photographs and complete the completion report truthfully. P1 emergency jobs require you to confirm when the site is made safe. You must follow site access and hazard instructions and work safely.</p>
  <h3>5. Invoicing and payment</h3>
  <p>You invoice <strong><%= company.legal_name %> trading as <%= company.trading_name %></strong>, never the customer, at your agreed rate card. GST-registered contractors must provide valid taxable supply information. We check invoices against the job, your rates and the evidence, and pay approved invoices on your agreed payment terms. Deductions are only made with your agreement.</p>
  <h3>6. Customer relationship and confidentiality</h3>
  <p>Customer information is confidential and used only to complete the job. You must not solicit Ridgeline's customers for maintenance work introduced through Ridgeline during the term and for [period to be confirmed] afterwards.</p>
  <h3>7. General</h3>
  <p>[To be completed with legal advice: liability and indemnity, workmanship warranty and remediation, termination, dispute resolution, governing law (New Zealand).]</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
